-- title:
--   Weil restriction of a closed subscheme along a finite flat morphism
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a commutative ring and let $C$, $W$ be schemes, all in a single universe $u$. Let $c : C \to \operatorname{Spec} S$ be a morphism which is finite, flat and locally of finite presentation, and let $w : W \to C$ be a closed immersion which is locally of finite presentation. The assertion is that there exists an ideal $J \subseteq S$ which is finitely generated and which has the following universal property: for every commutative ring $T$ (again in universe $u$) and every ring homomorphism $\psi : S \to T$, the first projection $\operatorname{pr}_1 : C \times_{\operatorname{Spec} S} \operatorname{Spec} T \to C$ of the pullback of $c$ along $\operatorname{Spec}(\psi)$ factors through $w$ — that is, there is a morphism $\ell : C \times_{\operatorname{Spec} S} \operatorname{Spec} T \to W$ with $w \circ \ell = \operatorname{pr}_1$ — if and only if the ideal of $T$ generated by $\psi(J)$ is the zero ideal, equivalently $J \subseteq \ker \psi$. No uniqueness of $\ell$, and no scheme structure on the locus, is asserted: the statement is the bare equivalence between factorisation of the projection and the vanishing of $J$ in $T$.
--
--   This is the representability, in ideal-theoretic form, of the Weil restriction (restriction of scalars) of a closed subscheme $W \subseteq C$ along a finite locally free morphism $c$ over an affine base: the functor sending an $S$-algebra $T$ to the condition '$W$ absorbs the whole of $C$ after base change to $T$' is cut out by a finitely generated ideal $J \subseteq S$, the content ideal of the ideal defining $W$ relative to a finite projective presentation of $\Gamma(C,\mathcal O_C)$ over $S$. It is used in the construction of fake elliptic curves in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd setting, where it supplies the finitely generated ideal detecting preservation of level structures under base change.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_exists_ideal_fg_forall_exists_comp_eq_pullback_fst_iff_map_eq_bot_of_isFinite_of_flat.lean

